WEBVTT

00:00:04.213 --> 00:00:06.256
One, two! One, two, three!

00:00:32.157 --> 00:00:35.077
You're entering a realm
which is unusual.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.039
Maybe it's magic
or contains some kind of monster.

00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:42.292
The second one. Prepare to enter...

00:00:45.504 --> 00:00:48.423
Please send the man round back
and pick up Clyde Smith,

00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:52.052
a professional gambler who's about to have
an unfortunate accident.

00:01:02.521 --> 00:01:05.399
A casino where I'm winning?

00:01:05.482 --> 00:01:09.319
That car must have killed me.
I must be in heaven.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:16.643
A casino where I always win?
That's boring.

00:01:16.727 --> 00:01:19.521
I must really be in hell!

00:01:19.604 --> 00:01:22.190
No, Mr. Smith,
you're not in heaven or hell.

00:01:22.274 --> 00:01:24.776
You're on an airplane.

00:01:26.445 --> 00:01:29.990
There's a gremlin destroying the plane!
You've gotta believe me!

00:01:30.073 --> 00:01:32.659
Why should I believe you? You're Hitler!

00:01:32.743 --> 00:01:36.413
No! Eva Braun, help me!

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.040
Ahhh!

00:01:38.749 --> 00:01:42.252
- Saw it comin'.
- I just saw something incredibly cool,

00:01:42.336 --> 00:01:46.089
a big floating ball that lit up
with every color in the rainbow,

00:01:46.173 --> 00:01:48.300
plus some new ones that were so beautiful,

00:01:48.383 --> 00:01:51.053
I fell to my knees and cried.

00:01:51.136 --> 00:01:53.221
Was it out in front of
Discount Shoe Outlet?

00:01:53.305 --> 00:01:54.473
Yeah.

00:01:54.556 --> 00:01:57.017
They have a college kid
wear that to attract customers.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:00.354
Well, I don't care
if it was just some dork in a costume.

00:02:00.437 --> 00:02:03.565
For one brief moment,
I felt the heartbeat of creation,

00:02:03.648 --> 00:02:05.651
and it was one with my own.

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:09.112
- Big deal.
- We all feel like that all the time,

00:02:09.196 --> 00:02:11.365
but you don't hear us gassin' on about it.

00:02:11.448 --> 00:02:13.450
How can you people be so blasé?

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:15.535
Here you are in the year 3000 or so,

00:02:15.619 --> 00:02:18.664
yet you just sit around
like it's the boring time I came from.

00:02:18.747 --> 00:02:22.834
"Boring"? Wasn't that the period
when they cracked the human genome

00:02:22.918 --> 00:02:25.170
and boy bands roamed the earth?

00:02:25.253 --> 00:02:27.964
Yeah, but now it's the distant future.

00:02:28.048 --> 00:02:30.634
Why aren't we out
doing everything I ever dreamed of?

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:34.221
- Hey, you know what might be a hoot?
- No. Why would I know that?

00:02:34.304 --> 00:02:36.306
Let's take the rest of the morning off

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:38.892
and take Fry to do everything
he ever wanted to do.

00:02:38.975 --> 00:02:41.061
- Everything?
- Except that.

00:02:44.314 --> 00:02:48.276
So's your fantasies has always been
to destroys a planet, huh?

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.904
Yeah. What did they ever do for me?

00:02:56.159 --> 00:03:00.789
Wow. The most humdrum activities
seem almost exciting through your eyes.

00:03:00.872 --> 00:03:03.709
- What should we do next?
- I wanna see the edge of the universe.

00:03:03.792 --> 00:03:05.711
Ooh. That sounds cool.

00:03:05.794 --> 00:03:07.754
It's funny. You live in the universe,

00:03:07.838 --> 00:03:11.008
but you never do these things
till someone comes to visit.

00:03:14.011 --> 00:03:17.139
There it is,
the edge of the universe.

00:03:31.236 --> 00:03:32.821
Far out.

00:03:32.904 --> 00:03:35.574
So there's an infinite number
of parallel universes?

00:03:35.657 --> 00:03:37.117
No. Just the two.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.619
Oh, well, I'm sure that's enough.

00:03:39.703 --> 00:03:43.290
I'm sick of parallel Bender
lording his cowboy hat over me.

00:03:43.373 --> 00:03:45.625
Let's move on to Fry's next fantasy.

00:03:49.129 --> 00:03:50.380
Yee-haw!

00:03:50.464 --> 00:03:52.883
Bow before your master, puny mortals!

00:03:53.175 --> 00:03:57.721
Whoo! Giddy-up! Ha, ha! Whoo! Whoopie!

00:03:57.971 --> 00:04:01.892
- Mommy? Why is that man like that?
- Don't look at him.

00:04:03.018 --> 00:04:05.187
That was fun. Let's give him a treat.

00:04:15.697 --> 00:04:17.491
Keep your palms flat.

00:04:21.411 --> 00:04:22.704
The tongue tickles.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.838
These new hands are great.
I'm gonna break 'em in tonight.

00:04:31.922 --> 00:04:34.049
Yes, it's been quite an hour and a half.

00:04:34.132 --> 00:04:35.967
I've only got two fantasies left,

00:04:36.051 --> 00:04:38.053
